3. COMMERCIAL USE RESTRICTIONS
================================================================================
ANY USE OF THE SOFTWARE FOR COMMERCIAL, REVENUE-GENERATING, FOR-PROFIT, OR
ENTERPRISE OPERATIONAL PURPOSES IS STRICTLY PROHIBITED WITHOUT A SEPARATE,
DIRECTLY EXECUTED REZONATOR COMMERCIAL LICENSE.

Specifically:
a. Financial Institutions & Banking: Any deployment, integration, or execution
   of the Software by or on behalf of banks, credit unions, clearing houses,
   hedge funds, insurance corporations, fintech providers, or their contractors
   requires a paid Rezonator Commercial License.
b. Enterprise Migration & Consulting: Any systems integrator, consultancy, or
   cloud vendor (including but not limited to IBM, Kyndryl, Accenture, AWS,
   Microsoft, or Big 4 advisory firms) analyzing client codebases with the
   Software must hold a valid commercial license.
c. SaaS & Network Hosting: Hosting the Software as an internal microservice,
   web API, remote analysis hub, or cloud SaaS offering for commercial users
   is expressly prohibited under the free tier.

================================================================================
4. PUBLIC HEALTHCARE & LIFE-SAVING HUMANITARIAN EXEMPTION
================================================================================
The copyright holder recognizes the imperative to protect life-critical and
acute emergency healthcare systems:

a. Royalty-Free Public Healthcare Waiver:
   Accredited public non-profit healthcare institutions, national public health
   services (including National Health Service (NHS) trusts in the UK), public
   university medical centres, emergency major trauma units, and intensive care
   units (ICU) may request and receive a 100% royalty-free, perpetual commercial
   use waiver for direct patient care, clinical operations, and life-critical
   hospital infrastructure upon written application to the copyright holder.

b. Exclusion of For-Profit Med-Tech Corporations:
   For-profit medical technology conglomerates, proprietary hospital software
   vendors, commercial electronic health record (EHR) corporations, and private
   for-profit clinic networks are expressly EXCLUDED from this humanitarian
   waiver. Such entities are classified as commercial users under Section 3 and
   must acquire a commercial license.

